[background arg="res://assets/Scene_Overlay.png" fade="0.0"]
join Lizzy (Close Up) right
Lizzy: VALERIE!
join Valerie (Close Up) left
Valerie: Ah, Elizabeth, how was your last day of highschool?
Lizzy: You said that yesterday.
Valerie: Oh. Did I? I think I would remember something like that.
Lizzy: You also mentioned something about faxing me class lists. It was a bad day in all honesty.
...
Valerie: Hm. You are under a lot of stress, so it makes sense that you would feel overwhelmed by—
Lizzy: No, you don’t understand.
Lizzy: I’m reliving the same day over again.
Lizzy: All exactly the same.
Lizzy: Maybe not exactly the same. There’s little differences.


set {current_decision} = GameState.spoken_today["barb"]
if {current_decision} == true:
	Lizzy: Barb, Noah, and Juniper didn't remember yesterday either.
	Valerie: Perhaps you're experiencing Deja vu? The sensation of feeling you’ve lived the same moment—
	Lizzy: I know what deja vu is and this is not it.
	Lizzy: I had to sit through the same two hour math exam I've already done.
	Lizzy: no one should have to go through that!
	Lizzy: It's evil!
else:
	Lizzy: but it's basically the same day!
	Valerie: Perhaps you're experiencing Deja vu? The sensation of feeling you’ve lived the same moment—
	Lizzy: I know what deja vu is and this is not it.
	Lizzy: I’m experiencing the same twenty-four hours over again.
	Lizzy: I got the same postcard from my mom and it's sort of overcast outside and we're having this conversation again!
	Lizzy: well, you don't remember what I said yesterday at least.
	Lizzy: you showed me your watch.
Valerie: The Keepers often hold committee meetings about these supernatural phenomena,
Valerie: and they often result in quite a few fists flying...
Valerie: Are you positive it's not the stress from graduation making you feel as though you're repeating the day?
Lizzy: Val, please, level with me.
Lizzy: Somebody has got to be behind this!
Lizzy: Somebody like Lady MacDeath, she raised a bunch of zombies in the last yesterday and was cackling about some evil plan.
Lizzy: like maybe she's trapping me in some sort of...
Lizzy: time circle, you know,
Lizzy: repeating it over and over again.
Valerie: you seem to be describing a time loop.
Lizzy: well,
Lizzy: maybe not a time loop.
VO: could be a time loop.
VO: oh god,
VO: I hope i'm not stuck in a time loop.
Valerie: One of the keepers, Humprey Egbert, the second, actually published a case study about this very thing.
do GameState.learn_fact("v_case_study")
VO: Oh no, she’s going off on one of her tangents.
Valerie: In the report he asserted that he’d been through more than ten years of the same day looping over and over again.
Valerie: It contained a very exhaustive list of citations and appendices,
Valerie: due in part because he had written it while being stuck in said time loop.
Valerie: The control group in this case was the rest of the world.
Lizzy: okay, well, how does this help me?
Valerie: I just thought it was interesting.
Lizzy: Maybe can you call Humphrey up and he can walk me through his repeating day.
Lizzy: we could compare notes.
Valerie: I detest phones.
Valerie: but in any case, we wouldn’t be able to.
Lizzy: Why not??
Valerie: He died.
Lizzy: oh.
Valerie: While on a sailing trip...
Valerie: The circumstances were quite mysterious and I’m still convinced he was murdered...
Valerie: No one will give me the funding to look into it.
Lizzy: This was a waste of time.
Valerie: Elizabeth, please know that I’m here to help with whatever problem you’re facing,
Valerie: but you need to be more realistic.
Valerie: Why would Lady MacDeath go to all the trouble to make a time loop when you could spend all of your loops figuring out how to stop her?
Lizzy: because she’s evil?
Valerie: You cannot create problems to solve. Change is scary and that's okay—
Lizzy: I'm not making this up, it's real.
Lizzy: We deal with weird stuff all the time, why is this so hard to believe.
Valerie: When I graduated from highschool, I was expected to go directly into the Keepers.
Valerie: It was tradition.
Valerie: but I didn't want to be a keeper. I saw how it tore my mother and father apart.
Valerie: the long hours, the desperate struggle between good and evil,
Valerie: and also the corruption within the institution.
Valerie: I don't like sharing this about myself, but...
Valerie: during my highschool years I'd worked a couple of odd jobs here and there at chemists and one stop shops.
Valerie: Eventually I'd saved up enough travel money.
Valerie: After I finished school, I packed a few things and took a train to Glasgow.
Valerie: that's in Scotland, if you were wondering.
Lizzy: I actually was.
Valerie: I left a note for my father, telling him I was going to live my own life and forge my own path.
Valerie: it was quite mean spirited actually.
Lizzy: This is kinda blowing my mind right now, Val.
Valerie: I am a very different person now.
do GameState.learn_fact("v_future_worries")
Lizzy: what did you do in Scotland?
Valerie: well, I mostly hung out with sheep in fields and wrote poetry while staring out at the water.
Lizzy: ...
Valerie: It took about two years for my father to finally track me down and take me back home.
Valerie: and I went kicking and screaming,
Valerie: but eventually,
Valerie: I saw reason.
Valerie: He sat me down and gave me this.
join "Strike Ball" (Watch) center [animation="Fade In Up"]
Valerie: This watch belonged to my great-great-grandmother, back when the Keep was first started.
Valerie: It's a symbol of the struggle between light and darkness.
Valerie: and why I had to join the Keepers.
leave "Strike Ball" [animation="Fade Out Down" length="0.3"]
Lizzy: The watch is nice and all, but you told me this last time too.
Valerie: I want you to hold onto it for me,
Valerie: just until graduation.
Valerie: then you can give it back.
Lizzy: I....
set {collected_item_name} = "Pocket Watch"
do GameState.pick_up_item("pocket_watch")
Lizzy: Thanks.
Valerie: get some rest before your big day.
Valerie: I'll see you tomorrow.
VO: if there is a tomorrow...



do ProgressionTracker.complete_requirement("1A", "library_dialog")
do GameState.mark_characters_as_spoken(["valerie"])
jump item_collected/